Check Failure Threshold Database <code>fail</code>: <code>/sante</code> answers 503 the database does not answer a basic query Last successful backup <code>warn</code> more than 26 hours (daily backup at 03:15) Last scheduled tasks <code>warn</code> more than 2 hours (run every hour) Free space on the <code>var/</code> disk <code>warn</code> less than 512 MiB New version <code>warn</code> a more recent version is published (daily check, if enabled) <p>A warning keeps the answer at 200: the application remains usable. The age of the backup comes from a marker file that the backup script writes in <code>var/supervision/</code> (the application has no access to the archive folder); the scheduled tasks write their own at every run. As long as one of them has never succeeded, its check stays in warning.</p> <p>Latest published version: disabled by default, Patrimeter then calls nothing outside. With <code>UPDATE_CHECK_URL</code> (address of the GitLab API of the latest Release, for instance <code>https://gitlab.example.org/api/v4/projects/56/releases/permalink/latest</code>) and, for a private project, <code>UPDATE_CHECK_TOKEN</code> (access token with the <code>read_api</code> scope, Reporter role), a scheduled task asks for it every day. A more recent version is reported once by email to <code>ADMIN_EMAIL</code>, then by the <code>update:available</code> check and the <code>patrimeter_update_available</code> metric until the update.</p> <pre><code>{
  "status": "pass",
  "checks": {
    "database:responseTime": [{"status": "pass", "observedValue": 0.41, "observedUnit": "ms"}],
    "backup:age": [{"status": "pass", "observedValue": 21340, "observedUnit": "s"}],
    "scheduler:age": [{"status": "pass", "observedValue": 1250, "observedUnit": "s"}],
    "disk:free": [{"status": "pass", "observedValue": 21474836480, "observedUnit": "bytes"}],
    "update:available": [{"status": "pass", "observedValue": null}]
  }
}
</code></pre>
